WEBVTT

00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.010
Only ten percent of your brain?

00:00:02.020 --> 00:00:03.845
A famous brain claim.

00:00:03.858 --> 00:00:05.556
Whole movies are built on it.

00:00:05.566 --> 00:00:09.370
In 1908, psychologist
William James wrote that

00:00:09.380 --> 00:00:11.420
people use only a small part of

00:00:11.430 --> 00:00:14.837
their possible mental
and physical resources.

00:00:14.847 --> 00:00:16.709
But in that essay, he never gave

00:00:16.719 --> 00:00:17.514
a number.

00:00:17.524 --> 00:00:21.239
The ten percent was popularised in 1936,

00:00:21.249 --> 00:00:23.689
in the preface of a bestselling self-help

00:00:23.699 --> 00:00:24.368
book.

00:00:24.378 --> 00:00:25.428
The catch:

00:00:25.478 --> 00:00:27.031
your brain is a few percent of

00:00:27.041 --> 00:00:29.106
your weight, but burns about a fifth

00:00:29.116 --> 00:00:30.252
of your energy.

00:00:30.262 --> 00:00:32.380
Keeping ninety percent of it switched off

00:00:32.390 --> 00:00:33.837
would make no sense.

00:00:33.847 --> 00:00:37.024
Brain scans show activity right across it,

00:00:37.034 --> 00:00:38.857
just not every part at once.

00:00:38.867 --> 00:00:41.010
Over a day, you use virtually all

00:00:41.020 --> 00:00:42.034
of your brain.

00:00:42.044 --> 00:00:44.247
The ten percent never came from brain

00:00:44.257 --> 00:00:45.344
science.
